                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pretty straight-forward story (due to the urgency of the plot) with some really interesting twists and lots of branching paths to choose from (that will lead you to your death, most likely). \r\n\r\nVery few artwork in the book, however. Which is a bummer. Same goes for the soundtrack (only two pieces of music available). But they are good, anyway. \r\n\r\nBut it's annoying af when you face enemies who have more than 6 dices. \r\n\r\nFeels like such fights are built to make you lose because they take forever to end, when it comes to your turn and pretty damn quick to come to a closure, when it's theirs, even when cheating the dices.\r\n\r\nThankfully, there are only two or three of such fights available in the game (and the last boss ain't one of them).\r\n\r\nGame is also pretty short. Managed to beat it twice in under 3 hours.",
